# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Hyper — environment template. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in real values.
#
# This file is committed on purpose, so it must never contain a real credential:
# no connection string with a password, no access key, no bucket name. Values
# below are placeholders. `.gitignore` excludes `.env*` and whitelists only this
# file, which means anything pasted here is published to everyone with repo
# access and stays in Git history forever.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Database ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Any PostgreSQL connection string — see DATABASE.md for provider guides
# (Neon, Prisma Postgres, RDS, Railway, local, zero-Docker local via
# `npm run db:local`, …).
#
# Use the DIRECT endpoint, not the pooled one. The app runs DDL on boot
# (`src/lib/migrate.ts`), and a pooled connection drops it mid-statement —
# which surfaces as `Connection terminated unexpectedly` or Prisma `P1017`,
# not as a clear "wrong endpoint" error. Providers label the two differently:
# Prisma Postgres uses `pooled.db.prisma.io` for pooled and `db.prisma.io`
# (or `aws-0-<region>.pooler.supabase.com` vs `.pooler.` for Supabase) —
# check the host, not the label.
DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:5432/DATABASE?sslmode=require

# Only for local/self-hosted Postgres WITHOUT TLS:
# DATABASE_SSL=false

# ── Runtime mode ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Force the app into read-only demo mode with no database queries —
# useful for UI work without a reachable cluster. Either variable works.
# FORCE_OFFLINE_MODE=true
# DB_MODE=offline

# Optional, and leave it unset in production. The app refuses to auto-seed the
# five demo accounts in production unless this is exactly `true`; seeding a
# live site with demo profiles puts app-owned accounts in front of real ones.
# ALLOW_DEMO_SEED=true

# ── Auth ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Authentication uses opaque, database-backed Prisma sessions. No auth secret
# is required; keep DATABASE_URL reachable so sessions can be created/read.

# ── Group video/audio calls ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# Group calls use native peer-to-peer WebRTC. The browser connects peers
# directly; Postgres only relays signaling (who is in the call, and the
# SDP/ICE messages). No third-party provider or API key is required.
#
# STUN-only is used by default. For NAT traversal across most networks an
# ICE/TURN server is recommended; add it by overriding the ICE servers in
# src/components/Call/WebRTCRoom.tsx.

# ── Media / object storage ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. When set, uploads go to a Prisma Object Store bucket (or any
# S3-compatible store: R2, MinIO, AWS S3). Postgres still stores only the
# stable URL `/uploads/<uuid>.<ext>` — never a presigned link.
#
# Prisma Console → your project → Object Store → create a bucket → mint a
# read_write key. The key response maps 1:1 onto these variables
# (bucketName, endpoint, accessKeyId, secretAccessKey).
#
# Leave all of these unset for local-disk uploads under public/uploads.
# S3_ENDPOINT=https://YOUR-STORAGE-HOST
# S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=YOUR-ACCESS-KEY-ID
# S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=YOUR-SECRET-ACCESS-KEY
# S3_BUCKET=YOUR-BUCKET-NAME
# S3_REGION=auto
# S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true
#
# Aliases accepted: PRISMA_BUCKET_NAME, PRISMA_BUCKET_ENDPOINT,
# PRISMA_BUCKET_ACCESS_KEY_ID, PRISMA_BUCKET_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY,
# PRISMA_BUCKET_REGION.

# ── Public site / SEO ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Canonical production origin, used for every canonical URL, the sitemap and
# Open Graph tags. Do not use a Vercel preview hostname.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://your-production-domain.example

# Optional public privacy-request inbox. Publish only a monitored address.
# PRIVACY_CONTACT_EMAIL=

# ── Web push ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. VAPID public key for browser push notifications
# (src/lib/notifications.ts). Without it push subscription is disabled.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_VAPID_KEY=

# ── Keys this app no longer reads ─────────────────────────────────────────
# RAPIDAPI_KEY and DAILY_API_KEY appear in older `.env` files but nothing in
# `src/` reads either one — RapidAPI only survives in a test asserting the key
# is never surfaced in the UI, and Daily was removed with the TURN integration.
# They are deliberately absent here. If a live key for either service is still
# in your `.env`, revoke it: an unused credential is pure exposure.
